.TH GLINT 1 "2026-10-19" "glint 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glint \- play a short event animation as a Wayland overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glint
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glint
draws a one-shot, click-through animation on a fullscreen
.B zwlr_layer_shell_v1
overlay surface and exits as soon as the last frame is shown.
It does no event detection itself; another tool, such as
.BR sysaud (1),
launches it when something happens.
.PP
The compositor must support the wlr layer-shell protocol (Hyprland, Sway,
river, niri and other wlroots-based compositors).
The layer surface namespace is
.BR glint ,
for compositor layer rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-animation " NAME"
Animation to play. Default:
.BR sparkle\-surge ,
a port of Android's wired-charging ripple.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration\-ms " MS"
Animation length in milliseconds. Default: 1750.
.TP
.BI \-\-primary\-color " COLOR"
Tint as
.B #RRGGBB
or
.BR #RRGGBBAA .
Default: #fff0b4.
.TP
.BI \-\-origin " POSITION"
Where the animation starts, for example the side of the charging port:
.BR top\-left ", " top ", " top\-right ", " left ", " center ", " right ", "
.BR bottom\-left ", " bottom " or " bottom\-right .
Default: bottom.
.TP
.BR \-\-all\-monitors " [" true | false ]
Draw on every monitor, or only the first one with
.BR false .
Default: true.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.SH EXAMPLES
Play the charging ripple from the bottom right corner in a light blue:
.PP
.RS
.nf
glint \-\-origin bottom\-right \-\-primary\-color '#7dd3fc'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run it from
.BR sysaud (1)
when a charger is connected, in
.IR ~/.config/sysaud/config.yaml :
.PP
.RS
.nf
events:
  power.ac\-plugged:
    script: glint \-\-origin bottom\-right
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after the animation finished, non-zero if Wayland or the layer-shell
protocol is unavailable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysaud (1)
.PP
https://github.com/anisthdev/glint
